---
code: cli-unknown-flag-did-you-mean
when-fires: an unrecognized flag that IS within edit-distance 2 of a real one. cli/lib.rs parse_args_from. {flag} is the token, {suggestion} the nearest real flag.
why: AID-NEEDS:law-codes-vary-by-world-not-grammar: the sibling of cli-unknown-flag, split by a WORLD-STATE (the flag table has a near neighbour) with its own remediation.
edit-loop: edit a sentence in the transcript below, then run `mise run loom:compile -- cli-unknown-flag-did-you-mean && mise run loom:promote -- cli-unknown-flag-did-you-mean`; prove it stuck with `mise run test`, which is also what catches anything else the promotion moved. `mise run loom:vars -- --all cli-unknown-flag-did-you-mean` lists this case's values; type {{name}} to insert or move one.
---
-- replay --
$ dorc plan --wat --book=webhost.sh
dorc: error[cli-unknown-flag-did-you-mean]: sm unknown flag `--wat` -- did you
mean `--last`?
usage: dorc [probe|plan|apply] --book=<book.sh> [-o <oracle.sh>]... [--debug-argv]
